3. UN-BOOTSTRAPPED CATEGORY STATE — traced against real code, then fixed
=========================================================================

Read normalizeProducts() in site-content.ts in full rather than trusting a
summary: today's 8 live categories carry no stored `id`, but DO get a
read-time FALLBACK `slug` (storedSlug || dedupeSlug(slugify(title), seen)).
Consequence, traced precisely:
  - Every one of the 8 real categories renders as an ENABLED <option> in the
    picker (disabled={!c.slug} is false for all of them) — only a category
    added fresh THIS session (ObjectListEditor's blank(), no slug key at
    all) would render disabled. The dispatch's phrasing ("disabled <option>
    for a slug-less category") describes a real, correctly-implemented, but
    narrower case than "all 8 today" — the amber banner, not the disabled
    option, is what today's 8 actually hit.
  - selectedSlug's initializer (`categories.find(c => c.slug)?.slug ?? ""`)
    picks the FIRST category, which — since all 8 have a fallback slug —
    means a category IS auto-selected on page load today. Combined with
    bootstrapped = Boolean(selected?.id) being false for all 8, **the amber
    banner is the first thing rendered in this card on page load, with zero
    clicks**, exactly as the dispatch says. Confirmed by direct trace of the
    real function, not assumed.

Copy judgment: already clear and actionable as written — names the specific
category, states the fix in one click ("no other changes needed"), tells
the editor to come back. No wording change made.

Fixed a real icon/role inconsistency: the banner was amber (this codebase's
established non-blocking-advisory color, per ImageUploadField's warning
state) but used TriangleAlert + role="alert" (this codebase's established
red HARD-ERROR icon/role, used identically in 3 other places in this same
file for genuine save failures). Changed to Info + role="status" +
aria-live="polite" — matching amber's OTHER existing pairing exactly
(ImageUploadField's non-blocking size/shape warning), rather than a color/
icon combination that appears nowhere else in the app. Nothing failed here;
this is a proactive notice shown before the editor has attempted anything,
which is the closer fit for status/info than for alert. Kept TriangleAlert +
role="alert" + red untouched everywhere it already correctly signals a
genuine failure (reorderError, AddProductForm's error, ProductRow's error) —
per the dispatch's own instruction to keep that language consistent with
SettingsHeader/ImageUploadField, which it already was and still is.

